From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: describe the DSU cluster PMU

Add an arm,dsu-pmu node, so the in-tree arm_dsu_pmu driver binds and
perf gets the DSU's L3, snoop-filter and bus event counters
(arm_dsu_0/...). Without them the DSU devfreq policy has no counter
source: its effect can be seen only as a switch count, and nothing
separates L3 starvation of the A76 from core frequency.

- interrupts: nCLUSTERPMUIRQ is INTID 274 = SPI 242 (A733 UM V1.00,
  chapter 12, interrupt sources table, vector 0x0448). Level: the DSU
  holds nCLUSTERPMUIRQ asserted while an overflow flag is set (DSU TRM
  100453 B3); GIC SPIs take level-high or rising edge only, and the
  SoC-side inversion is not documented, so level-high is the one
  setting a stimulus can prove -- an overflow that is counted exactly
  once per period in /proc/interrupts.
- cpus: all eight cores; CLUSTERCFR reads 8 cores in one DSU on silicon
  (read on the board, 2026-09-29).

The vendor device tree has no such node, so this is not a port.

Depends on the BL31 change allwinner-a733-el2-access-to-the-dsu-cluster-pmu:
the kernel runs at EL2 (VHE) and the cluster PMU registers trap to EL3
unless ACTLR_EL3[12] is set (DSU TRM B3.4 "Traps and enables"). On a
chain without it, the driver's first register access traps.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -463,6 +463,21 @@
 	};
 
 	/*
+	 * DSU cluster PMU (L3, snoop filter, bus), one instance for all
+	 * eight cores. nCLUSTERPMUIRQ is INTID 274 = SPI 242 (UM
+	 * V1.00 chapter 12, interrupt sources table).
+	 * The counters are reachable from EL2 only
+	 * because BL31 sets ACTLR_EL3[12] on every core
+	 * (allwinner-a733-el2-access-to-the-dsu-cluster-pmu).
+	 */
+	dsu-pmu {
+		compatible = "arm,dsu-pmu";
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 242 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		cpus = <&cpu0>, <&cpu1>, <&cpu2>, <&cpu3>,
+		       <&cpu4>, <&cpu5>, <&cpu6>, <&cpu7>;
+	};
+
+	/*
 	 * SYS_CLK24M -- the SoC-internal 24 MHz that every peripheral block
 	 * calls "hosc". It is NOT the crystal on this board and it does not
 	 * follow it:
